      "description": "Watch Bologna vs Lazio highlights and goals from Serie A on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 24, 2026. The Stadio Renato Dall'Ara played host to a high-stakes tactical battle on August 24, 2026, as Bologna and Lazio locked horns in a crucial Serie A encounter. Both managers set up their sides with discipline, resulting in a match where every inch of turf was contested with immense physical intensity. A Gritty Opening Exchange The first half was defined more by defensive organization and refereeing intervention than attacking fluidity. Early bookings set the tone, with Romano Floriani Mussolini receiving a yellow card in the 22nd minute for a rough challenge. Tempers flared further in the 34th minute when Boulaye Dia and Oussama El Azzouzi were both cautioned for unsportsmanlike conduct. While Bologna looked to use their home advantage, clear-cut chances were rare, and Lazio goalkeeper Christos Mandas remained alert to keep out a goal-bound header from Eivind Helland just before the interval. Frattesi Breaks the Deadlock The decisive moment of the match arrived in the 59th minute. In a swift move that caught the Bologna defense momentarily out of position, Boulaye Dia turned provider, setting up Davide Frattesi with a perfectly weighted pass. Frattesi made no mistake, firing a right-footed shot into the net to give Lazio the lead. This goal prompted a tactical reshuffle from the hosts, as they introduced Artem Dovbyk and Federico Bernardeschi in an attempt to spark a comeback. Late Drama and Defensive Heroics As the clock ticked down, the pressure on the Lazio goal reached a fever pitch. In the 77th minute, Bologna thought they had found the equalizer when Eivind Helland beat the keeper, only to see his effort heroically cleared off the goal line. The tension remained high until the final whistle, with late yellow cards for Jens Odgaard , Torbjoern Lysaker Heggem , and Oliver Provstgaard highlighting the desperation on both sides. Despite controlling 59% of possession, Bologna could not find a way through the resilient Roman defense, as Lazio held on for a hard-fought victory."
